"""Verified generalized-Sudoku generators for arXiv:1210.6343.

The paper represents a generalized Sudoku by three permutations that divide
``n^2`` cells into ``n`` groups of size ``n``.  A solution assigns the symbols
1,...,n once to every group.  Theorem 5.1 reconstructs such a solution from the
sign vector of one permuted comparison matrix.

This module inverse-generates a cyclic gerechte design, hides its field
coordinates behind independent permutations, and publishes the row comparison
signs.  The answer is the four coefficients of an inverse-affine symbolic
solution.  Expanding that formula gives all ``n^2`` Sudoku entries, which the
verifier checks locally and exactly.

Generation is deterministic in ``(n, seed, params)``.  There is no file I/O,
