The paper establishes worst-case parameterized hardness, but also polynomial-time solvability on tree hosts ([paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2209.08757)). The retained star-host construction passed all local G/V gates, yet the bare oracle solved 9/9 attempts:

- `q=1009`: 3/3
- `q=2003`: 3/3
- `q=4001`: 3/3

The mechanical reference averaged 16,241 operations at `q=1009`; the compact projective route takes at most 92. Models consistently found that shortcut, so Track-B hardness fails. The `q=8009` run was unscored due to API quota errors.

